   the justification;

A domain is defined by coherent
function: what enters, what changes, what is owned, what is guaranteed,
what leaves, and what adjacent domains can rely on

- the effective blanket is a low-rank projection in the representation
  space along which object identity is preserved under treatment;
- the attribute basis is evidence for that projection; the projection is
  not a column-membership predicate;

- decide on its own what the next state will be after a user event;
- chain several state updates locally without emitting them as separate
  Msg values;
- carry hidden inter-event state in refs, closures or module-level
  variables.

- an initial State fixture;
- an ordered Msg log;
- the expected final State;
- the expected ordered Cmd values;
- the success and failure Msg values returned by interpreted Cmds;
- injected deterministic values for time, randomness, generated ids and
  external payloads.

